{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,29]],"date-time":"2026-05-29T10:47:35Z","timestamp":1780051655670,"version":"3.53.1"},"reference-count":57,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Ltd","issue":"26","funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001691","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["18H04484"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["18H04484"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001691","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001691","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["18H01216"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["18H01216"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001691","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Int. J. Mod. Phys. A"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2021,9,20]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> The index theorems relate the gauge field and metric on a manifold to the solution of the Dirac equation on it. In the standard approach, the Dirac operator must be massless to make the chirality operator well defined. In physics, however, the index theorem appears as a consequence of chiral anomaly, which is an explicit breaking of the symmetry. It is then natural to ask if we can understand the index theorems in a massive fermion system which does not have chiral symmetry. In this review, we discuss how to reformulate the chiral anomaly and index theorems with massive Dirac operators, where we find nontrivial mathematical relations between massless and massive fermions. A special focus is placed on the Atiyah\u2013Patodi\u2013Singer index, whose original formulation requires a physicist-unfriendly boundary condition, while the corresponding massive domain-wall fermion reformulation does not. The massive formulation provides a natural understanding of the anomaly inflow between the bulk and edge in particle and condensed matter physics. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142\/s0217751x21300155","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,10,8]],"date-time":"2021-10-08T20:35:07Z","timestamp":1633725307000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":4,"title":["Understanding the index theorems with massive fermions"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"36","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8406-1649","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hidenori","family":"Fukaya","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Physics, Osaka University, Machikane-Yama-Cho 1-1, Toyonaka 560-0043, Japan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2021,10,8]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB001","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1090\/S0002-9904-1963-10957-X"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB002","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2307\/1970715"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB003","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0305004100049410"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB004","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0305004100051872"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB005","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0305004100052105"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB006","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRev.177.2426"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB007","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF02823296"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB008","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevD.13.3398"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB009","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0550-3213(85)90489-4"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB010","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0370-2693(92)91112-M"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB012","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s00220-020-03806-0"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB013","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/ptep\/ptaa031"},{"key":"S0217751X21300155BIB015","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"1